* BD-2-style overdrive (the classic blue-pedal kind), from a hobbyist redraw of the 2001 schematic (rev 3): a JFET input buffer, two discrete gain stages (a JFET differential
* pair into a PNP common-emitter stage, used as an op-amp) with the dual-gang GAIN pot in their feedback and a four-diode clipper between them, a passive TONE, the LEVEL pot,
* an op-amp stage with a gyrator in its inverting leg and the output buffer. 9 V supply, the op-amp references at 4 V (VB).
*
* Gain stages: the BD2_STAGE op-amp (open loop gain about 700, 2.2k output resistance, 7 MHz gain-bandwidth: the pair's gm and the 2.2k loads) with the + input from the 100n / 2.2n
* couplings (220k / 1M to 4 V) and the - input on the feedback node: 1.5k with 150n (stage 1; 2.2k with 1u in stage 2) to ground, and the feedback through 22k (33k in stage 2)
* plus the GAIN section (250k log, VRG1 and VRG2) with 47p (100p) across it. Between the stages: 100k, 220p / 330k, 100n, 47n, 1M and 15k into the clipping node M, which has two
* diodes in series each way to ground (D1..D4, 1N914) and the 2.2n coupling into stage 2.
* Tone: 5.6k with 5.6n, 18n, the 10k TONE pot with 18n at its bottom, then LEVEL (100k log) and 47n into the third op-amp (M5218, 4558 type): 6.8k with 2.2n in the feedback, the two
* diodes across its inputs, and in the inverting leg the gyrator (56n, 1.2k, a follower on 5.6n / 470k with 10k).
* Switching (the effect on / off JFETs and the bypass buffer) is left out: the effect path is always connected. The buffers (the JFET at the input, the NPN at the output) are ideal
* followers, the input is loaded like the real one (2.2M at the jack, 1M gate bias).
* Assumptions: the BD2_STAGE numbers (the JFET gm and the PNP gain are not printed on the drawing); the bottom end of the GAIN pots is open; the 150n of stage 1 is read as printed;
* the diodes across the third op-amp's inputs are both drawn pointing the same way (as read).

V VB vb 1 4
C CB vb 0 47u

I VIN gin 1
R RIN gin 0 2.2M
C C1 gin a 47n
R R2 a g0 10k
R R3 g0 vb 1M
O UJ g0 nj q vb TL072_9
R RJF q nj 1
R RJL q 0 10k

* Into stage 1 (the effect-on JFET as a closed switch).
C CB1 q n1 1u
R RN1 n1 vb 1M
R RSW n1 n2 300
R RN2 n2 vb 1M
C C100 n2 n3 100n
R RN3 n3 vb 220k

* Stage 1.
O S1 n3 f1 o1 vb BD2_STAGE
R RG1 f1 g1 1.5k
C CG1 g1 vb 150n
R VRG1 o1 w1 1
R R22 w1 f1 22k
C CF1 f1 o1 47p

* The network and the clipper between the stages.
R RP o1 p1 100k
C CP1 p1 m 100n
C C220 o1 c22 220p
R R330 c22 m 330k
C C47 p1 q1 47n
R R1M m q1 1M
R R15K q1 0 15k
D D1 m d1 SIGNAL
D D2 d1 0 SIGNAL
D D3 0 d2 SIGNAL
D D4 d2 m SIGNAL

* Stage 2.
C CS2 m n4 2.2n
R RN4 n4 vb 1M
O S2 n4 f2 o2 vb BD2_STAGE
R RG2 f2 g2 2.2k
C CG2 g2 vb 1u
R VRG2 o2 w2 1
R R33 w2 f2 33k
C CF2 f2 o2 100p

* Tone and level.
R RT5 o2 ta 5.6k
C CT56 o2 ta 5.6n
C CT18 ta tb 18n
R VRT_T tb tw 1
R VRT_B tw tg 1
C CT18B tg 0 18n
R VRL_T tw lv 1
R VRL_B lv 0 1
C C47B lv l 47n
R RL l vb 10M

* The third op-amp: feedback 6.8k with 2.2n, the two diodes across its inputs, the gyrator in the inverting leg.
O S3 l f3 o3 vb RC4558
R R68 f3 o3 6.8k
C C22N f3 o3 2.2n
D D5 f3 l SIGNAL
D D6 f3 l SIGNAL
C C56N f3 gy 56n
R R12K gy ne 1.2k
C C56B gy gb 5.6n
R R470K gb vb 470k
O UG gb ng ne vb TL072_9
R RGF ne ng 1
R RE10 ne vb 10k

* Output: 10u, the switch JFET (closed) with its 1M bias, 1u into the NPN buffer (100k bias), 10u, 10k and the 1k to the jack.
C C10 o3 x1 10u
R RX1 x1 vb 1M
R RSW2 x1 x2 300
R RX2 x2 vb 1M
C C1B x2 x3 1u
R RX3 x3 vb 100k
O UB x3 nb xb vb TL072_9
R RBF xb nb 1
R RB10 xb vb 10k
C C10B xb xo 10u
R RXO xo 0 10k
R R1K xo y 1k
R RLOAD y 0 100k
